{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nlimit = 6000\nsieve = [True] * limit\nsieve[0] = False\nsieve[1] = False\nfor i in range(2, int(limit ** 0.5) + 1):\n    if sieve[i]:\n        for j in range(i * i, limit, i):\n            sieve[j] = False\nprimes = [i for i in range(2, limit) if sieve[i]]\n\ndef factor(n):\n    d = {}\n    for p in primes:\n        if p * p > n:\n            break\n        if n % p == 0:\n            cnt = 0\n            while n % p == 0:\n                n //= p\n                cnt += 1\n            d[p] = cnt\n    if n > 1:\n        d[n] = 1\n    return d\n\ndef divisors(n):\n    divs = [1]\n    for p, e in factor(n).items():\n        divs = [old * p ** k for old in divs for k in range(e + 1)]\n    return divs\n\ndef process(n, m):\n    f = {0: 0, 1: 1, 2: 2}\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        total = 2 * f[i - 1]\n        for x in divisors(i):\n            if 2 <= x <= i:\n                total += f[i // x] - f[(i - 1) // x]\n        f[i] = total % m\n    return f[n]\n\nn, m = [int(x) for x in input().split()]\nprint(process(n, m))\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <map>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst int LIMIT = 6000;\nvector<int> primes;\n\nvoid sieve() {\n    vector<bool> is_prime(LIMIT, true);\n    is_prime[0] = is_prime[1] = false;\n    for (int i = 2; i * i < LIMIT; ++i) {\n        if (is_prime[i]) {\n            for (int j = i * i; j < LIMIT; j += i) {\n                is_prime[j] = false;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    for (int i = 2; i < LIMIT; ++i) {\n        if (is_prime[i]) primes.push_back(i);\n    }\n}\n\nmap<int, int> factor(int n) {\n    map<int, int> res;\n    for (int p : primes) {\n        if (p * p > n) break;\n        if (n % p == 0) {\n            int cnt = 0;\n            while (n % p == 0) {\n                n /= p;\n                ++cnt;\n            }\n            res[p] = cnt;\n        }\n    }\n    if (n > 1) res[n] = 1;\n    return res;\n}\n\nvector<long long> divisors(int n) {\n    map<int, int> fac = factor(n);\n    vector<long long> divs = {1};\n    for (auto &entry : fac) {\n        int p = entry.first;\n        int e = entry.second;\n        vector<long long> new_divs;\n        long long pk = 1;\n        for (int k = 0; k <= e; ++k) {\n            for (long long old : divs) {\n                new_divs.push_back(old * pk);\n            }\n            pk *= p;\n        }\n        divs = new_divs;\n    }\n    return divs;\n}\n\nlong long process(int n, int m) {\n    vector<long long> f(n + 1);\n    f[0] = 0;\n    f[1] = 1;\n    f[2] = 2;\n    for (int i = 3; i <= n; ++i) {\n        long long total = (2 * f[i - 1]) % m;\n        vector<long long> divs = divisors(i);\n        for (long long x : divs) {\n            if (x >= 2 && x <= i) {\n                long long term = f[i / x] - f[(i - 1) / x];\n                term %= m;\n                if (term < 0) term += m;\n                total = (total + term) % m;\n            }\n        }\n        f[i] = total;\n    }\n    return f[n];\n}\n\nint main() {\n    sieve();\n    int n, m;\n    cin >> n >> m;\n    cout << process(n, m) << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-3.671578815556131e-05, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0004611144249793142, -0.001994050806388259, -1.2040065485052764e-05, -0.04868418723344803, -1.4781842764932662e-05, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.0728830375228426e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -0.6214107871055603, -3.909988299710676e-05, -3.540453326422721e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.12703755497932434, -0.12696333229541779, -0.061973441392183304, 0.0, -0.005297314375638962, -0.062005262821912766, -0.008450583554804325, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, -1.3828182090946939e-05, -0.01195056363940239, -0.00012385078298393637, -0.001412823679856956, -9.60780744208023e-05, -2.622600959512056e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -0.20192867517471313, -0.00014256415306590497, -0.20401211082935333, 0.0, -0.000723576988093555, -0.004514146130532026, -0.018162252381443977, -0.03498287498950958, -0.001209600013680756, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -3.6954811548639555e-06, -0.0002485204895492643, -2.9802276912960224e-06, 0.0, -0.00012134769349358976, -0.0015301911626011133, -7.867782187531702e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -0.00012814177898690104, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -9.536738616588991e-07, 0.0, -2.1219027985353023e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -0.2014141082763672, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, -0.0015023384476080537, -1.0132738680113107e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.6689160474925302e-05, -2.264974000354414e-06, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, -4.172316494077677e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.030693281441926956, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.07888985425233841, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 